// universe per parent UNIVERSE-PURE dispatch 58cae91 (rmw3 S5 Option A —
// 1,404 ¬ live; audit v0.5 — cleanup set = 123 canon rows: P1-P110 +
// P129-P132 + P281-P289; the 166 artifact rows P111-P128/P133-P280 are
// NOT cleanup targets).
// Each observation: observed map evidence ✓ cost → options → recommendation
// → target-doc (exact § where a change would land, IF ruled) → gate.
// NOT canon. No canon edit in this task (g5): target mapping only.

proposals("VSL-NOTATION-REVIEW-PROPOSALS") {

  // ════ OBSERVATION 1 (the one rmw3 asked to share — FULL AUDIT DONE) ════
  obs("O1_negation_glyph") {
    observed: "
      The ¬ glyph (U+00AC) is declared in the alphabet (core_boot_primer
      notation + primer §3) and used heavily as a PROSE-fix: ¬covers, ¬new,
      ¬re-stated, ¬duplicated, ¬LLM, ¬a boot read, ¬there, ¬sibling…
      It is mathematically standard (logical negation) BUT as a prose prefix
      it is not standard notation anywhere else — every new reader must
      recondition '¬' = 'not' before the corpus is legible.",
    evidence: "
      COMPLETE audit ran five times — v0.1 (existential, 2026-08-12), v0.2
      (UNIVERSE-FIRST reverse census, 2026-08-13 per parent recorrection),
      v0.3 (instrument-versioned, canon universe, 2026-08-13), v0.4 (FULL
      agreed universe, 2026-08-13 per parent UNIVERSE-EXTEND dispatch
      7e02136) and v0.5 (CANON-PURO, 2026-08-13 per parent UNIVERSE-PURE
      dispatch 58cae91) — see not_usage_audit.vsm in this task. Universe:
      1,404 ¬ across 73 carrying files (canon 949/47 + spec-sandbox 138/4
      + ledger 76/1 + child_docs 57/5 dispatches + child_sandbox 184/16
      canon vsl-language-rev+README; EXCLUDED: vsl-notation-review/*
      self-census artifacts + the defining dispatch). Verdict:
        • 20 uses = LOGICAL (1.4%); 8 of them REAL canon logical negation
          over formulas (0.8% of canon): L1-L6 (vos_core_theory
          ¬(H = H_rest @always); hard_rules ¬( build(C)∘ dev_host ),
          ¬( deploy(..) ), ¬( state(C)∘host_root∖exceptions ),
          ¬∃ such check ⟹; core_boot_primer ¬{parse_json}) + L7/L8 found by
          the reverse census (s5_policy_annex ∧ ¬Δ(architecture);
          core_boot_primer ∧ ¬Δid). The other 12 LOGICAL are child canon
          rows (dispatch envelopes quoting the same formula syntax +
          language-rev primer).
        • 4 uses = glyph tables (0.3%): 3 canon (vsl_language:37,
          vsl_language:33, core_boot_primer:38) + 1 child canon
          (vsl_language_primer:135). v0.2's T4 (child sandbox mirror) was
          outside the v0.3 universe — corrected; in v0.4 the dir IS in the
          universe (gate 4); v0.5 drops the artifact tables (self-census).
        • 1,239 uses = ¬word prose-affix (88.2%) — shorthand, NOT ambiguous.
        • 141 uses = PROSE-AMBIGUOUS (10.0%) in the script's canon-puro
          total, of which the 123 CLEANUP rows (P1-P110 + P129-P132 +
          P281-P289) are listed in not_usage_audit.vsm §5; the other 18 are
          child_docs dispatch hits (counted in the universe, NOT cleanup
          targets per gate 2). v0.2 said 33 — the old instrument's verb
          regex dropped 77 real 'do ¬' rows; the versioned script
          (tools/not_census.py v0.6) prints the complete canon-puro set.
      rmw3's hypothesis is now answered: the corpus is 88.2% prose
      shorthand; real logical use exists and is 0.8% of canon, all
      inside rule/axiom formulas. My v0.1 '3 cleanup sites' claim was
      WRONG — existential self-check, not universal census. Fixed in
      v0.2; the set grew to 110 in v0.3 with the corrected instrument,
      to 289 in v0.4 with the full universe, and is 123 CANON rows in
      v0.5 canon-puro (the artifacts are not canon to promote).",
    cost: "
      Orientation cost ~1 re-read per new agent; the glyph is NOT monovalent
      (proven: 8 real canon formulas + 123 ambiguous canon prose sites). A
      reader cannot assume ¬ is always prose-affix; 123 sites are
      structurally confusable (do ¬touch, ¬'quote', ¬(a), ¬3, ¬10×, ¬φ↓).
      The cleanup set is exactly the 123 canon rows in the audit — the
      parent's re-audit mandate. CANON-facing cleanup is the full 123-row
      set (P1-P110 system+sandbox + P129-P132 child canon + P281-P289
      ledger); the 166 artifact rows (P111-P128 dispatch envelopes +
      P133-P280 vsl-notation-review self-census) are NOT canon edits — they
      are transitory records, excluded per the canon-puro universe.",
    options: [
      "A — keep glyph, ADD usage note in §alphabet + primer §3:
          '¬P = logical operator over a formula (¬(…), ¬∃, ¬{…}, ∧ ¬Δ(…)) —
          formula context only; ¬word = prose prefix for NOT-word',
          2-line addition; corpus text unchanged",
      "A′ — A + clean the 123 CANON PROSE-AMBIGUOUS sites (P1-P110 +
          P129-P132 + P281-P289): rephrase the verb-shorthand (do ¬touch →
          'does not touch'), ¬'quote' → not-'…', ¬digit → 'not 3', etc.
          123 edits, surgical, verified list in audit (the 166 artifact
          rows P111-P128/P133-P280 stay — they are transitory records,
          not canon)",
      "B — corpus-wide rename prose-affix to 'non-'/'not' — breaks every
          affected doc (1,242 sites), high churn, NOT recommended",
      "C — keep as-is, document the convention only in ONE place (README/howto)",
    ],
    recommendation: "A + A′ — the usage note (2 lines) PLUS the canon 123-site
      cleanup (P1-P110 + P129-P132 + P281-P289, verified). Preserves the 8
      genuine canon logical uses and 3 canon glyph tables; kills the reading
      tax at every ambiguous canon site. The v0.1 claim of '3 sites' is
      retracted — the real canon-puro set is 123, of which the full set is
      cleanup.",
    target_doc: "
      IF ruled: boot/vsl_language.vsm §alphabet (glyph entry) +
      boot/vsl_language_primer.vsm §3 alphabet (glyph entry) — 2 lines
      each. Cleanup edits: the 123 canon sites (P1-P110 across 30 files,
      P129-P132 child canon 4 files, P281-P289 ledger 1 file — listed in
      not_usage_audit.vsm §5). 8 REAL canon logical uses + 3 canon glyph
      tables stay untouched.",
    gate: "parent S4 ruling (single-loop read, no behavior change) → if
      accepted as canon-text, rmw3 S5 approval before edit (double-loop:
      boot package is canon).",
  }

  // ════ OBSERVATION 2 — the two-tier structure ════
  obs("O2_operational_vs_theory") {
    observed: "
      definitions D1-D13 are operational (recursion, signals, adjustment,
      trust) while D14-D21 are theory (split operator, softmax mixing,
      filtration, seqlock) — the reader hits the tier boundary with ¬marker
      (they are one contiguous list in canon §2; my reference set split them
      into two files, but the files' NAMES don't say why).",
    evidence: "
      canon §2 lists D1..D21 contiguously; D14's own comment 'addendum
      2026-05-09' is the only tier signal. In the reference set I split
      definitions_core (D5-D13+D11b) / definitions_theory (D14-D21) — the
      split is real but unmotivated on the face.",
    cost: "
      A reader grabbing D19 VR_complex from 'definitions' expects the
      operational register (how the system adjusts) and gets topology math.
      Two registers under one name = wrong expectation ~once per reader.",
    options: [
      "A — add a one-line TIER comment at the top of each definitions group:
      'OPERATIONAL tier (D1-D13): what the running system does' /
      'THEORY tier (D14-D21 addendum): the math underneath proofs' — 2 lines",
      "B — rename definitions_theory.vsm → theory_definitions.vsm to signal
      register in the filename",
      "C — keep as-is (canon organizes by ID ¬by register)",
    ],
    recommendation: "A (+ optionally B) — tiny, kills the expectation mismatch.",
    target_doc: "
      IF ruled: boot/vsl_language.vsm §2 definitions (tier comments) +
      sandbox set definitions_core.vsm / definitions_theory.vsm headers.",
    gate: "parent S4 ruling; canon edit needs rmw3 S5 (double-loop).",
  }

  // ════ OBSERVATION 3 — declared-vs-implemented aging ════
  obs("O3_liveness_markers") {
    observed: "
      A definition can sit in canon while the kernel runs something else —
      D11b stayed canonical though superseded by D17 (its own comment says
      '? SUPERSEDED BY D17, and ¬implemented'); D6 needed a CORRECTED note
      after a wrong reading; the parser BNF was stale for months. The
      markers exist ad hoc (SUPERSEDED/CORRECTED/RESOLVED) but they are
      prose comments, ¬a uniform field — a reader cannot tell at a glance
      what is LIVE.",
    evidence: "
      canon §2 D11b '? SUPERSEDED BY D17'; D6 'CORRECTED 2026-08-07'; §7b
      grammar 'RESOLVED 2026-08-09'; §17 PSI 'WORKING VALUE — calibrates'.
      Four different phrasings for (roughly) 'this is not the number/source
      of truth right now'.",
    cost: "
      Orientation tax per definition: read the formula, read its comment,
      infer liveness. Miss one caveat → trust a dead formula (the R4
      discipline exists precisely because this happened).",
    options: [
      "A — introduce a uniform optional field @live ∈ {implemented, superseded,
      calibrating, declared-only} per definition/axiom; comments stay as
      prose, but the field is machine-checkable (symbol_table can flag a
      definition with ¬@live)",
      "B — audit + normalize the existing comment vocabulary (SUPERSEDED →
      one canonical wording) — cheaper, ¬machine-checkable",
      "C — keep as-is (R4 vigilance is the process)",
    ],
    recommendation: "B first (cheap, immediate), A as a separate later RFC
      (needs grammar/validator change = bigger gate).",
    target_doc: "
      IF ruled: boot/vsl_language.vsm §2 definitions (uniform marker) +
      §7b grammar (stale-closure note) + sandbox set items headers.",
    gate: "parent S4 ruling; any canon edit or grammar change → rmw3 S5
      (double-loop; @live field would touch the notation spec itself).",
  }

  // ════ SUMMARY ════
  summary: "
    Three observations, three smallest-viable-change recommendations:
    O1 → ¬ audit v0.5 INSTRUMENT-VERSIONED done (not_usage_audit.vsm,
    CANON-PURO universe 1,404 ¬): 8 real canon logical uses, 1,239
    prose-affix (88.2%), 123 canon PROSE-AMBIGUOUS cleanup rows listed
    (P1-P110 + P129-P132 + P281-P289; script total 141 — the other 18 are
    dispatch records, not cleanup targets) of which ALL are canon-facing —
    v0.1 '3 sites' claim RETRACTED; v0.2's '33' corrected to 110 once the
    versioned instrument (tools/not_census.py) enumerated every ¬ (the old
    regex dropped 77 'do ¬' rows); v0.4 extended to the full universe per
    UNIVERSE-EXTEND dispatch 7e02136; v0.5 trimmed to canon-puro per
    UNIVERSE-PURE dispatch 58cae91 — recommend usage note (A) + canon
    123-site cleanup (A′), preserving the logical uses. O2 → tier comments
    (2 lines, applied in sandbox). O3 → normalize liveness vocabulary
    (B applied as LIFESTATUS, A deferred). ¬one requires re-architecting; all three are
    orientation-friction fixes the parent can rule on independently. If the
    parent rules accept on any, that ruling goes to rmw3 (S5) for the canon
    edit; the sandbox carries the mapping until then.",
}
